      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Good Morning!"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "text": "The British Council is accused of glorifying terrorist attacks against Israel after providing funds to the Palestinian Museum in Birzeit, West Bank."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "text": "Christie’s 20th-century art evening sale at Rockefeller Center totaled $626.6 million including fees."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "text": "A dinosaur fossil that sat in a drawer at London’s Natural History Museum for nearly a century, has been identified as a previously unknown species."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The Headlines"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "TERROR’S TREASURY. The British Council has provided public funding to the Palestinian Museum in Birzeit, West Bank, which has been accused of glorifying terrorist attacks against Israeli civilians, The Telegraph reports. Exhibits include posters depicting Dalal al-Mughrabi, who led the 1978 Coastal Road massacre in which 38 Israelis were killed, as a martyr, alongside material celebrating Hamas bomb-maker Yahya Ayyash. UK Lawyers for Israel has called for funding to be suspended and an investigation launched. The Charity Commission has opened a regulatory compliance case into Taawon UK, a charity linked to the museum. The British Council says it is reviewing the allegations, while Taawon denies wrongdoing.",
