    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "TEPID RESULT AT CHRISTIE’S. As ARTnews reported, Christie’s 20th-century art evening sale at Rockefeller Center raised $626.6 million including fees. The 74-lot auction was led by a Wassily Kandinsky abstraction, which sold for $85.8 million, followed by a Gustav Klimt landscape at $82.3 million. The sale’s hammer total was $521.1 million, just above the low estimate. Five works were withdrawn before the auction, including a Frida Kahlo painting estimated at $2–3.5 million, which was pulled just hours before proceedings began.",
