    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The UK government has placed an export ban on Mughal calligraphy works valued at £900,000 and delayed the export of an 18th-century marble bust of Edward the Black Prince , to give a British museum the opportunity to acquire it. [ UK Gov ] Harvard’s Peabody Museum has returned the remains of a man and woman, believed to have been enslaved, to Brazil after more than 150 years in its collection. [ The Art Newspaper ] Simon O’Donovan, a National Museum of Ireland staffer charged with possessing an improvised explosive device, is seeking the return of his car and other property seized by the police. [ Irish Times ]",
